---
permalink: /internal/home-concepts/
noindex: true
title: "Home concepts | Internal review, Tajima Ramen"
description: "Internal review page. Three alternate home page directions on one document, switched in place. Not a shipping page and not linked from the site."
---
{#
  ===========================================================================
  REVIEW PAGE. NOT A SHIPPING PAGE.

  Built in response to a client note from Andy on the current home preview:
  "Is it possible to have the website to be simpler, less crowded, and clean
  look. We also feel there are repetitive information across the website."

  WHAT IS ACTUALLY ON THE CURRENT HOME PAGE (src/index.njk), counted rather
  than remembered:

    Sections, in order: hero, stat bar, Noodle Room card, location router,
    menu teaser, curtain-stage film, story. Seven, plus header and footer.

    THREE <video> elements, not two, and two of them are the same file:
    tajima-san-diego-web-background-full.mp4 plays behind the hero AND behind
    the Noodle Room card. The curtain stage is the third and plays a
    different film (tajima-brand-video-web-1080p.mp4).

    ONE fully duplicated stat block. site.stats renders 25 / 6 / 2 / 1 in the
    stat bar, and site.footer.spec renders the same four figures with almost
    the same labels inside the monolith footer, one scroll apart. (Both are
    the CORRECTED figures. The "8 houses / 12h tonkotsu" version was the
    reference concept's and never shipped; see the _statsNote in site.json.)

    FOUR texture and glow layers stacked over the content: the site-wide
    paper grain on body::before, the hero panel's two diagonal stripe fields
    plus its night radial glow, .pattern-section on the story section, and
    the monolith's atmospheric radial.

    FOUR Noodle Room mentions: the hero's secondary CTA, the Noodle Room card
    (heading plus its own inline CTA), the menu teaser's note line, and the
    footer nav.

    The location list is SEVEN rows, not six. Maui is in locations.json.

  So the read holds in substance and misses on the details: three videos not
  two, four texture layers not two, seven location rows not six, and the
  duplicated stats are 25/6/2/1 rather than the concept's uncorrected set.

  WHAT THIS PAGE IS. Three directions, all simpler, switchable in place so
  they can be compared in one conversation rather than across three links.
  A changes canvas AND density. C changes density only, the control. B keeps
  the night canvas and answers the crowding with scale: the biggest type,
  the fewest moves. Whichever one Andy reacts to tells us which lever was
  doing the work.

  ROUND 2, per Steve's review of the first build: A read poorly (its note
  rows floated as unanchored text, fixed with the card treatment), the first
  B was a light/dark banded scroll that sat too close to A (replaced
  entirely with the bold night take), and C was closest to the target
  (touched least). See each concept's own comment.

  WHAT THIS PAGE DOES NOT TOUCH: src/index.njk, its route, nav.json,
  site.json, DESIGN_SYSTEM.md, voice-tone.md. The live home page is exactly
  as it was.

  COPY RULE FOLLOWED THROUGHOUT: every sentence here is lifted from
  src/index.njk or from the approved examples in voice-tone.md, trimmed or
  reordered. Nothing is newly written except where marked NEW LINE, and no
  Sam quote appears in any concept. The H1 is the locked web hero primary in
  all three.

  FACT BUDGET. The acceptance rule for this review is that no stat or fact
  appears twice inside one concept, since that is the client's second
  complaint. Each concept below carries a ledger showing where each fact
  landed. Menu prices are treated as menu data from menu.json rather than as
  stats, and A drops them entirely.

  DELETE THIS FILE, src/css/pages/home-concepts.css, its import in app.css,
  src/js/pages/home-concepts.js, and the two theme.css system constants once
  a direction is chosen.
  ===========================================================================
#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html
  lang="{{ site.locale }}"
  data-mode="{{ site.theme.mode }}"
  data-fonts="{{ site.theme.fonts }}"
  data-pattern="{{ site.theme.pattern }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

  <title>{{ title }}</title>
  <meta name="description" content="{{ description }}">

  {# Unlinked and unindexed. There is no sitemap in this build to exclude it
     from (nothing generates one yet), and public/_headers carries a matching
     X-Robots-Tag for /internal/* so the rule survives even if this tag is
     ever lost in a refactor. #}
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow">

  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://cdn.circulationstudio.com" crossorigin>
  <link
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bebas+Neue&family=Barlow+Condensed:ital,wght@0,300;0,400;0,600;0,700;1,600&family=Barlow:wght@300;400;500;600&display=swap"
    rel="stylesheet">

  {# Concept A is the default, so its hero photograph is the LCP element on
     first paint. B and C are hidden and are not preloaded: preloading an
     image inside a hidden panel would compete with the real LCP for
     bandwidth, which is the exact trap the base layout's heroImage note
     warns about. #}
  <link rel="preload" as="image" href="/images/photo/tajima-ramen-convoy-traditonal-tonkotsu-04.webp" fetchpriority="high">

  <script type="module" src="/src/js/main.js"></script>
</head>

<body>

  {#
    Set up the three shared lists once. Every concept reads these, so a data
    change cannot drift between them.

    `where` twice rather than `selectattr`: Nunjucks' selectattr silently
    degrades to a truthiness check and returns every item whose key is set,
    which is a quiet wrong-output bug rather than an error. See the filter's
    own note in eleventy.config.js and TEAM_NOTE-nunjucks-selectattr.md.

    All seven featured ramen carry an image, so there is no empty-frame case
    to guard. Carnitas Ramen has feature: false in menu.json and is excluded
    here for the same reason it is excluded everywhere: it does not appear on
    this site.
  #}
  {%- set featuredRamen = menu.items | where("section", "ramen") | where("feature", true) %}

  <a class="skip-link" href="#hc-main-a">Skip to content</a>

  {# ==================== THE SWITCHER ====================
     First in the DOM so a keyboard user reaches it before a concept's
     header, fixed to the bottom of the viewport so it never covers the hero
     it is being used to judge. Three real buttons with aria-pressed. Nothing
     here removes focus from the page or holds it. #}
  <div class="hc-switch" role="group" aria-label="Home page concept" data-hc-switch>
    <span class="hc-switch__label">Concept</span>
    <div class="hc-switch__set">
      <button type="button" class="hc-switch__btn" data-hc-btn="a" aria-pressed="true">A &middot; Quiet craft</button>
      <button type="button" class="hc-switch__btn" data-hc-btn="b" aria-pressed="false">B &middot; Bold</button>
      <button type="button" class="hc-switch__btn" data-hc-btn="c" aria-pressed="false">C &middot; Direct</button>
    </div>
    <span class="hc-switch__note">Internal review</span>
  </div>


  {# =======================================================================
     CONCEPT A. Quiet Craft, on Off-White.

     The canvas variable, isolated, and the hardest cut of the three.

     CUT AGAINST THE CURRENT HOME: the stat bar, both background videos, the
     curtain-stage film (that story belongs on /about/), the pattern overlay,
     the story section's standalone treatment, the animated monolith footer
     and its duplicate stat strip. Seven sections become four.

     NOODLE ROOM: one mention, one link, per the brief. It stays because it
     is the growth priority and it is not droppable from any concept.

     FACT LEDGER, each appears exactly once:
       2001 and Convoy Street ... hero lede
       Crown Point, the machine from Japan ... Noodle Room note
       every morning, six San Diego locations ... menu note
       Sam still runs it ... the house note
     The three sentences are the approved home hero body from voice-tone.md,
     split across the page rather than stacked in one paragraph. No sentence
     is new.
     ======================================================================= #}
  <section class="hc-concept hc-a hc-light" data-hc-concept="a" aria-label="Concept A, quiet craft on Off-White">

    {% set megaInstance = "a-" %}
    {% include "components/site-header.njk" %}

    <main id="hc-main-a">

      <div class="hc-hero">
        <div class="hc-hero__copy">
          <span class="hc-hero__eyebrow">San Diego, California</span>

          {# The locked web hero primary from voice-tone.md. Do not write a
             new hero line at build time. #}
          <h1 class="hc-hero__title">
            <span>Better noodles</span>
            <span>weren't for sale.</span>
            <span><em>So we made them.</em></span>
          </h1>

          <p class="hc-hero__lede">
            Tajima has been on Convoy Street since 2001.
          </p>

          {# The one red fill on this concept. The header CTA is outlined
             inside .hc-light so the two never stack in one viewport. #}
          <a class="hc-cta" href="/locations/">Find your Tajima</a>
        </div>

        <figure class="hc-hero__figure">
          <img
            class="hc-hero__img"
            src="/images/photo/tajima-ramen-convoy-traditonal-tonkotsu-04.webp"
            alt="Traditional Tonkotsu Ramen, thin-sliced pork chashu, wood ear mushrooms, green onions and sesame seeds on pork bone broth"
            width="854"
            height="1280"
            loading="eager"
            fetchpriority="high">
        </figure>
      </div>

      {# ---------- The Noodle Room. One mention, one link. ---------- #}
      <section class="hc-note" aria-labelledby="hc-a-nr">
        <div class="hc-note__head">
          <span class="hc-note__eyebrow">The noodles</span>
          <h2 class="hc-note__title" id="hc-a-nr">The Noodle Room</h2>
          <p class="hc-note__body">
            The noodles are made in our own room in Crown Point, on a machine we brought over from Japan.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a class="hc-link" href="/noodle-room/">Step inside the Noodle Room</a>
      </section>

      {# ---------- Menu teaser. Component reused as-is. ----------
         Three bowls, names only. A is the hardest cut, and /menu/ carries the
         prices and the descriptions. #}
      <section class="menu" aria-labelledby="hc-a-menu">
        <div class="menu__inner">
          <header class="menu__head">
            <h2 class="menu__title" id="hc-a-menu">The <em>bowls.</em></h2>
            <p class="menu__note">
              The broth is simmered every morning and driven to all six San Diego locations.
            </p>
          </header>

          <div class="menu__grid">
            {%- for dish in featuredRamen %}
              {%- if loop.index <= 3 %}
            <article class="dish">
              <figure class="dish__figure">
                <img class="dish__img" src="{{ dish.image }}" alt="{{ dish.alt }}" loading="lazy" width="{{ dish.imageWidth }}" height="{{ dish.imageHeight }}">
              </figure>
              <div class="dish__meta">
                <h3 class="dish__name">
                  {%- if dish.emphasis -%}
                    {{ dish.shortName | replace(dish.emphasis, "") }}<em>{{ dish.emphasis }}</em>
                  {%- else -%}
                    {{ dish.shortName }}
                  {%- endif -%}
                </h3>
              </div>
            </article>
              {%- endif %}
            {%- endfor %}
          </div>

          <p class="menu__more">
            <a class="menu__more-link" href="/menu/">See the whole menu</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      {# ---------- Location router. Component reused, "Since" column cut. ---------- #}
      <section class="locations hc-locations--plain" aria-labelledby="hc-a-loc">
        <div class="locations__inner">
          <header class="locations__head">
            <h2 class="locations__title" id="hc-a-loc">Where to <em>find us.</em></h2>
            <a class="hc-link" href="/locations/">All locations</a>
          </header>

          {%- for loc in locations.items %}
          <article class="locations__row">
            <span class="locations__row-no">&#8470;&nbsp;{{ "0" if loop.index < 10 }}{{ loop.index }}</span>
            <h3 class="locations__row-name">
              <a href="{{ loc.url }}">{{ loc.name }} <em>{{ loc.descriptor }}</em></a>
            </h3>
            <address class="locations__row-addr">
              {%- if loc.address.street %}{{ loc.address.street }}, {% endif -%}
              {%- if loc.neighborhood and loc.neighborhood != loc.address.locality %}{{ loc.neighborhood }}, {% endif -%}
              {{ loc.address.locality }}, {{ loc.address.region }}
            </address>
          </article>
          {%- endfor %}
        </div>
      </section>

      {# ---------- The house. One line, link to /about/. ---------- #}
      <section class="hc-note" aria-labelledby="hc-a-house">
        <div class="hc-note__head">
          <span class="hc-note__eyebrow">The house</span>
          <h2 class="hc-note__title" id="hc-a-house">One owner</h2>
          {# TRIMMED, not new. src/index.njk reads "Sam Morikizono took over a
             small Japanese restaurant on Convoy Street in 2001 and has run it
             ever since." The place and the year are already in the hero, so
             only the part this section is for survives. #}
          <p class="hc-note__body">
            Sam Morikizono took it over, and has run it ever since.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a class="hc-link" href="/about/">Read how Sam got here</a>
      </section>

    </main>

    {# Stripped footer, not the monolith. See the .hc-close note in
       home-concepts.css: the monolith's spec strip is the duplicated stat
       block this concept exists to remove. #}
    <footer class="hc-close" aria-label="{{ site.name }} footer">
      <div class="hc-close__inner">
        <p class="hc-close__crest" aria-hidden="true">但馬</p>
        <nav class="hc-close__nav" aria-label="Footer">
          {%- for item in nav.footer %}
          <a href="{{ item.url }}"{% if item.external %} rel="noopener"{% endif %}>{{ item.label }}</a>
          {%- endfor %}
        </nav>
        <p class="hc-close__sub">{{ site.name }} &middot; {{ site.footer.region }} &middot; &copy; {{ buildYear }}</p>
      </div>
    </footer>

  </section>


  {# =======================================================================
     CONCEPT B. Bigger, Bolder, Simpler, on the night canvas.

     ROUND 2, rebuilt after Steve's review. The first B was a light/dark
     banded editorial scroll; his read was that it sat too close to A, with C
     closest to what the client wants. This B answers his note directly:
     night canvas kept, and the crowding complaint answered with SCALE, not
     with banding. Five moves:

       1. A full-bleed photographic poster hero, slogan at --text-display,
          one CTA, no video.
       2. The Noodle Room as a display-size statement, one sentence, one
          link. The growth priority gets the same scale as the hero.
       3. Three bowls, names and prices only.
       4. The location index: seven names at --text-h1, the list itself as
          the page's interface. The / brief says the visitor already knows
          Tajima and wants routing; B makes the routing the biggest thing
          on the page after the slogan.
       5. One line for Sam, then the monolith.

     CUT AGAINST THE CURRENT HOME: the stat bar, all three videos, the
     curtain-stage film, the pattern overlay, the story section, addresses in
     the location list (NAP lives on the location pages and /locations/).

     FACT LEDGER, each appears exactly once. B ends on the real monolith
     footer, so the footer holds the numbers and the hero holds none:
       25 / 6 / 2 / 1 ... the monolith spec strip
       Convoy, 2001 ... the monolith epitaph
       Crown Point, the machine from Japan ... Noodle Room statement
       every morning, before service ... menu note
       Sam still runs it ... the house card
     The hero is the slogan alone. No lede, same reasoning as C.
     ======================================================================= #}
  <section class="hc-concept hc-b" data-hc-concept="b" aria-label="Concept B, bigger and bolder on the night canvas" hidden>

    {% set megaInstance = "b-" %}
    {% include "components/site-header.njk" %}

    <main id="hc-main-b" hidden>

      {# ---------- The poster. One photograph, the slogan, one CTA. ----------
         Tajima Black: the darkest bowl in the featured set, shot in the
         room, so the night canvas reads as continuous with the photograph.
         Type on the photo uses system constants per the overlay rule.
         loading="lazy" because B is hidden on first paint and must not
         compete with A's LCP preload. #}
      <section class="hc-poster" aria-labelledby="hc-b-title">
        <figure class="hc-poster__media">
          <img
            class="hc-poster__img"
            src="/images/photo/tajima-ramen-convoy-tajima-black-03.webp"
            alt="Tajima Black ramen with black garlic oil and chashu over dark tonkotsu broth"
            width="1280"
            height="854"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async">
        </figure>
        <div class="hc-poster__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>

        <div class="hc-poster__inner">
          <span class="hc-poster__eyebrow">San Diego, California</span>

          <h1 class="hc-poster__title" id="hc-b-title">
            <span>Better noodles</span>
            <span>weren't for sale.</span>
            <span><em>So we made them.</em></span>
          </h1>

          {# Cream pill, red type: the shipped hero__order pattern. The
             header's Order Online pill is this viewport's one red fill. #}
          <a class="hc-poster__cta" href="/locations/">Find your Tajima</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      {# ---------- The Noodle Room, at display size. ---------- #}
      <section class="hc-band hc-band--dark" aria-labelledby="hc-b-nr">
        <div class="hc-band__inner">
          <div class="hc-band__lead">
            <h2 class="hc-band__title hc-band__title--big" id="hc-b-nr">The<br><em>Noodle Room</em></h2>
            <p class="hc-band__body">
              The noodles are made in our own room in Crown Point, on a machine we brought over from Japan.
            </p>
          </div>
          <p class="hc-band__foot">
            <a class="hc-link" href="/noodle-room/">Step inside the Noodle Room</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      {# ---------- Three bowls, names and prices only. ---------- #}
      <section class="menu" aria-labelledby="hc-b-menu">
        <div class="menu__inner">
          <header class="menu__head">
            <h2 class="menu__title" id="hc-b-menu">The <em>bowls.</em></h2>
            {# TRIMMED from index.njk's note. Crown Point is named in the
               statement above, "six" lives in the monolith, so neither
               repeats here. #}
            <p class="menu__note">
              Broth simmered every morning and driven out before service.
            </p>
          </header>

          <div class="menu__grid">
            {%- for dish in featuredRamen %}
              {%- if loop.index <= 3 %}
            <article class="dish">
              <figure class="dish__figure">
                <img class="dish__img" src="{{ dish.image }}" alt="{{ dish.alt }}" loading="lazy" width="{{ dish.imageWidth }}" height="{{ dish.imageHeight }}">
              </figure>
              <div class="dish__meta">
                <h3 class="dish__name">
                  {%- if dish.emphasis -%}
                    {{ dish.shortName | replace(dish.emphasis, "") }}<em>{{ dish.emphasis }}</em>
                  {%- else -%}
                    {{ dish.shortName }}
                  {%- endif -%}
                </h3>
                <span class="dish__price">${{ dish.price }}</span>
              </div>
            </article>
              {%- endif %}
            {%- endfor %}
          </div>

          <p class="menu__more">
            <a class="menu__more-link" href="/menu/">See the whole menu</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      {# ---------- The index. Seven names, giant, each row one link. ----------
         No addresses on purpose: the name and descriptor route, NAP lives on
         the location pages. The head label is the smallest type in the
         section because the rows are the headline. #}
      <section class="hc-index" aria-labelledby="hc-b-loc">
        <div class="hc-index__inner">
          <header class="hc-index__head">
            <h2 class="hc-index__label" id="hc-b-loc">Where to find us</h2>
            <a class="hc-link" href="/locations/">All locations</a>
          </header>

          {%- for loc in locations.items %}
          <article class="hc-index__row">
            <a class="hc-index__link" href="{{ loc.url }}">
              <span class="hc-index__no">&#8470;&nbsp;{{ "0" if loop.index < 10 }}{{ loop.index }}</span>
              <span class="hc-index__name">{{ loc.name }}</span>
              <span class="hc-index__tag">{{ loc.descriptor }}</span>
            </a>
          </article>
          {%- endfor %}
        </div>
      </section>

      {# ---------- One line for Sam. ---------- #}
      <section class="hc-note" aria-labelledby="hc-b-house">
        <div class="hc-note__head">
          <span class="hc-note__eyebrow">The house</span>
          <h2 class="hc-note__title" id="hc-b-house">One owner</h2>
          <p class="hc-note__body">
            Sam Morikizono took it over, and has run it ever since.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a class="hc-link" href="/about/">Read how Sam got here</a>
      </section>

    </main>

    {# The shipped footer. Its spec strip is the only place the 25 / 6 / 2 / 1
       figures appear in this concept, and the epitaph the only Convoy/2001. #}
    {% include "components/monolith.njk" %}

  </section>


  {# =======================================================================
     CONCEPT C. Direct and Practical, dark canvas unchanged.

     The control. No .hc-light anywhere, no colour change of any kind, the
     shipped .hero and .monolith reused exactly as they are. The only rule
     this concept adds is a height (see .hc-c .hero in home-concepts.css), so
     the location finder clears the fold.

     CUT AGAINST THE CURRENT HOME: the stat bar, the Noodle Room card, the
     curtain-stage film and its second video, the pattern-overlaid story
     section. Everything that used to be a full section inline is now one
     line and a door. Seven sections become three, and the duplicated stat
     block goes because the footer's copy is now the only one.

     If Andy still says "too dark" after seeing this next to A and B, the
     canvas was the complaint. If he says "still busy," it was not.

     FACT LEDGER, each appears exactly once. C is the only concept that keeps
     the monolith, so the footer holds more of the budget than in A or B and
     the hero holds none of it:
       25 / 6 / 2 / 1 ... the monolith spec strip
       Convoy, 2001 ... the monolith epitaph
       Crown Point, the machine from Japan ... Noodle Room door
       every morning, before service ... menu door
       Sam still runs it ... the house door
     The hero therefore carries no lede at all. See the note on it below.
     ======================================================================= #}
  <section class="hc-concept hc-c" data-hc-concept="c" aria-label="Concept C, direct and practical" hidden>

    {% set megaInstance = "c-" %}
    {% include "components/site-header.njk" %}

    <main id="hc-main-c" hidden>

      {# ---------- Hero. The shipped component, one video, shorter. ---------- #}
      <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hc-c-title">

        <div class="hero__video">
          <video
            class="hero__video-media"
            src="https://cdn.circulationstudio.com/tajima-temp/videos/tajima-san-diego-web-background-full.mp4"
            autoplay
            muted
            loop
            playsinline
            preload="metadata"
            data-decorative
            aria-hidden="true"></video>
          <div class="hero__video-scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="hero__panel">
          <div class="hero__panel-top">
            <img
              class="hero__logo"
              src="https://cdn.circulationstudio.com/tajima-temp/Tajima%20Branding/tajima%20brand%20assets_digital_RGB-07.png"
              alt="Tajima Ramen"
              width="200"
              height="120"
              loading="lazy">
            <span class="hero__eyebrow">San Diego, California</span>

            {# NO LEDE, and this is the one place where the fact budget and
               the density brief agree on the same cut.

               C is the only concept that keeps the monolith footer, and the
               monolith already states six of the facts a hero lede would
               reach for: 25, 6 San Diego, 2 noodle types, 1 Noodle Room in
               the spec strip, plus "Built in Convoy. Since 2001." in the
               epitaph. Every sentence of the approved hero body collides
               with one of them, so any lede here would be the second time
               this page said the same thing, which is the complaint.

               The three approved sentences are downstairs instead, one per
               door. The H1 and the location finder carry the top of the
               page, which is what "direct and practical" should look like
               anyway. #}
          </div>

          <h1 class="hero__display" id="hc-c-title">
            <span class="hero__display-line">Better noodles</span>
            <span class="hero__display-line">weren't for sale.</span>
            <span class="hero__display-line"><em>So we made them.</em></span>
          </h1>

          <div class="hero__panel-bottom">
            <div class="hero__actions">
              {# Unchanged from the live hero: cream-on-red inside the red
                 panel, so it is not a second red fill beside the header CTA.
                 The secondary points at /menu/ rather than /noodle-room/,
                 because C's single Noodle Room mention is prose below and
                 SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md asks for that link in body copy. #}
              <a class="hero__order" href="/locations/">Find your Tajima</a>
              <a class="hero__secondary" href="/menu/">See the menu</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </section>

      {# ---------- The location finder, immediately. ----------
         This is the change C is really making: the router used to be the
         fourth thing on the page, behind a stat bar and a video card. #}
      <section class="locations" aria-labelledby="hc-c-loc">
        <div class="locations__inner">
          <header class="locations__head">
            <h2 class="locations__title" id="hc-c-loc">Where to <em>find us.</em></h2>
            <a class="hc-link" href="/locations/">All locations</a>
          </header>

          {%- for loc in locations.items %}
          <article class="locations__row">
            <span class="locations__row-no">&#8470;&nbsp;{{ "0" if loop.index < 10 }}{{ loop.index }}</span>
            <h3 class="locations__row-name">
              <a href="{{ loc.url }}">{{ loc.name }} <em>{{ loc.descriptor }}</em></a>
            </h3>
            <address class="locations__row-addr">
              {%- if loc.address.street %}{{ loc.address.street }}, {% endif -%}
              {%- if loc.neighborhood and loc.neighborhood != loc.address.locality %}{{ loc.neighborhood }}, {% endif -%}
              {{ loc.address.locality }}, {{ loc.address.region }}
            </address>
          </article>
          {%- endfor %}
        </div>
      </section>

      {# ---------- Three doors. One line each, no section inline. ---------- #}
      <div class="hc-notes">

        <section class="hc-note" aria-labelledby="hc-c-nr">
          <div class="hc-note__head">
            <span class="hc-note__eyebrow">The noodles</span>
            <h2 class="hc-note__title" id="hc-c-nr">The Noodle Room</h2>
            <p class="hc-note__body">
              The noodles are made in our own room in Crown Point, on a machine we brought over from Japan.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a class="hc-link" href="/noodle-room/">Step inside the Noodle Room</a>
        </section>

        <section class="hc-note" aria-labelledby="hc-c-menu">
          <div class="hc-note__head">
            <span class="hc-note__eyebrow">The bowls</span>
            <h2 class="hc-note__title" id="hc-c-menu">The menu</h2>
            <p class="hc-note__body">
              Broth simmered every morning and driven out before service.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a class="hc-link" href="/menu/">See the whole menu</a>
        </section>

        <section class="hc-note" aria-labelledby="hc-c-house">
          <div class="hc-note__head">
            <span class="hc-note__eyebrow">The house</span>
            <h2 class="hc-note__title" id="hc-c-house">One owner</h2>
            <p class="hc-note__body">
              Sam Morikizono took it over, and has run it ever since.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a class="hc-link" href="/about/">Read how Sam got here</a>
        </section>

      </div>

    </main>

    {# The shipped footer, unchanged. Its spec strip is the only place the
       25 / 6 / 2 / 1 figures appear in this concept. #}
    {% include "components/monolith.njk" %}

  </section>

  <script type="module" src="/src/js/pages/home-concepts.js"></script>

</body>
</html>
